      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, that\u0027s the intent. `approx` holds a floating point value that we cast to integer (via `round` which returns an I32) then bit-pun back to float (via `pun_to_F32`). Every bit pattern from 0x7f800001 to 0x7fffffff is NaN, and past that we start dropping high bits and just get nonsense (or maybe `round` clamps to 0x7fffffff, I dunno, but that would still give NaN).",
