      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah. I had to read the code, then come back later once my brain had processed for a bit.\n\nJust looked at the implementation of `round` and it looks like there\u0027s no guarantee for what it does for out-of-range values. At least, for immediates, it calls lrintf. \n\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/math/rint : \"If the result of the rounding is outside the range of the return type, FE_INVALID is raised and an implementation-defined value is returned\"\n\nActually, that is a concern, it\u0027s not guaranteed to be consistent from run to run. We do want reproducible results.",
